From: Blakestream-GaintB V2.2
Subject: [PATCH] baikal: experimental per-board PLL indices

Add opt-in per-board PLL indices for logical boards 0..2. The options stay
off unless baikal-experimental-pll is set and baikal-clock-mode is exactly
individual. Each index is an integer 8..32; malformed, missing, and
conflicting values stop the process instead of being clamped. Normal mode
still sends index 30 for the public 400 label. Indices are not measured MHz.

GET_INFO readback uses the stock display table for every index 8..32. That
echo is not a calibrated frequency and does not prove the ASIC PLL locked.
Clock code 0 remains fan/thermal only. Experimental mode refuses the
bridge-global transport. A lab BAIKAL_RAW_CLOCK_CODE value cannot replace
the computed code.

API stats add ExperimentalClock and RequestedPLLIndex. RequestedPLLIndex is
0 when experimental mode is off; SentClockCode stays the code that was sent.
